# CCR (claude-code-router) was removed: it sat in Claude Code's hot path with
# no routing rules, so a dead router meant every session failed. These are the
# targets it left behind on machines that applied the old dotfiles.
.claude-code-router
.config/systemd/user/ccr-health.service
.config/systemd/user/ccr-health.timer
.local/bin/ccr-health

# The SSH-tunnelled microphone forward was retired: it only ever existed so
# Claude Code's CLI recorder could reach a client mic from a box that has no
# capture device, and the harness this machine now runs records on the phone
# instead. This is the target it left behind on machines that applied the old
# dotfiles.
.asoundrc

# The context7-mcp user skill duplicated the context7 plugin, which already
# registers the same MCP server and carries its own usage instructions.
.claude/skills/context7-mcp

# The /pr, /standup and /explain commands went unused: the shared rules and the
# no-mistakes pipeline already cover PR bodies, and none of the three was ever
# invoked in the session transcripts.
.claude/commands/pr.md
.claude/commands/standup.md
.claude/commands/explain.md

# The session-summary Stop hook was never wired into settings.json, and the
# statusline already shows the session's cost and duration.
.claude/hooks/session-summary.sh
